      },
      "title": "A page file",
      "description": "**What it is:** the page for **/chat**.\n\n**How it works:** a page is just the component a `page.tsx` file exports as `export default`. This one starts with `\"use client\"` (line 1) because it uses state and effects.\n\n**Why it matters:** this is where the chat screen starts. Tour 03 uses it for your React lesson.\n\n**Watch out:** the file is short on purpose. It loads your connected accounts, then hands everything to `ChatContainer`."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/app/(authenticated)/chat/[id]/page.tsx",
      "line": 35,
