      },
      "title": "Dynamic routes: [id]",
      "description": "**New idea — dynamic segments:** a folder name in square brackets matches *any* value. `chat/[id]/page.tsx` handles **/chat/abc123**, and `id` becomes `\"abc123\"`.\n\n**How it works:** Next.js passes the value in `params`. In Next.js 15 and 16, `params` is a **Promise**, so it's read with `await params` (line 20). That's why there's an `async` inner component wrapped in Suspense.\n\n**Why it matters:** each saved chat gets its own address that you can reload or share.\n\n**Watch out:** this file has no `\"use client\"`, so it's a server component. It passes the id to `ChatSessionClient`, which runs in the browser."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/app/(authenticated)/chat/loading.tsx",
      "line": 25,
      "selection": {
